  "note": "Self-written school trip notices to parents (a three-day school trip and a two-day outdoor school, in each language), each in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. The school trip letters run as business/email, since each is a letter (拝啓, Dear Parents and Carers); the outdoor school notices as business/press-release, the genre for public notices. There is no school genre. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line (or on its pairedLine). The cost per student times the number of students is a sentence in the school trip letters (line-amount-mismatch reads only tables, so it is named as the rule that should) and table rows in the outdoor school notices. The installments are a table or a list, with the trip fee stated apart and no total row; installment-total-mismatch is named as the rule that should add them up against the fee. The return date is a labelled line after the departure line in the letters (due-before-issue compares labelled pairs) and the end of one range in the notices (date-range-reversed). The payment deadline is a date in the payment table or list, after the trip's departure; deadline-after-event is named as the rule that should read the departure date as the event and a payment deadline as a deadline. The meeting time is a labelled line before the departure line, or a row of the day's schedule (time-order). yarn planted schooltrips scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
